```gitignore
# === Obsidian Vault Plugin/System Data ===
# Ignore the entire .obsidian folder, as it contains plugin configurations, cache, and metadata.
.obsidian/

# Ignore data generated by smart-env and other background services
.smart-env/
.local/

# Ignore compiled markdown/HTML/PDF exports (if these are done outside of structured notes)
**/*.html
*.json
*.ajson

# Ignore binary or serialized file types not intended to be tracked
*.sqlite
*.db

# === General Cache / Temp Files ===
# Operating system or temporary cache files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~

# Global Git ignores for Obsidian (optional, but good practice)
# Exclude internal database files
```



# Ignore Smart Environment folder
.smart-env

.obsidian/
*.sync-conflict
